1
00:00:00,174 --> 00:00:01,740
人工智能将把我们带向何方？
Where are we going with AI?

2
00:00:03,598 --> 00:00:11,620
我想我们今天会了解到，虽然并不完全确定，但我们确实在走向某个地方，而且速度非常快。
So I think we'll learn today, we're not exactly sure, but we are going somewhere and we're going somewhere fast.

3
00:00:12,398 --> 00:00:26,000
我从1994年左右就开始参与人工智能领域了，当时我在超新星分类程序中使用了双层神经网络。
So I've been involved with AI since about 1994 when I used a two-layer
neural network as part of my supernova classification program in 1994.

4
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:26,220
在那之前。
before.

5
00:00:26,560 --> 00:00:29,796
所以，我们现在处于一个完全不同的阶段。
So, we are now at something that is completely different.

6
00:00:30,560 --> 00:00:41,720
我刚在德国参加了一个叫作 Heidelberg Laureate Forum 的活动，
那里有 Fields Medalist 和 Abel Prize 得主、数学家，还有一群计算机科学家。
I was just in Germany with the Fields Medalist and Abel Prize winners, mathematicians,
and a bunch of computer scientists at something called the Heidelberg Laureate Forum.

7
00:00:42,960 --> 00:00:49,680
现在，这些数学家所经历的一切，是他们四个月前无法预料到的。
Now, what the mathematicians are experiencing right now, they were not expecting four months ago.

8
00:00:50,190 --> 00:01:02,260
从五月开始，大量未解决的数学难题突然有了解决
方案，这些解法是通过人工智能辅助编程产生的。
Starting in May, a huge number of unsolved problems in mathematics
have suddenly had solutions, emerged through AI-assisted programming.

9
00:01:03,660 --> 00:01:10,320
这让那群人——用澳大利亚人的话说——彻底震惊了。
And that has knocked that group, well, as we would say in Australia, for six.

10
00:01:10,440 --> 00:01:17,120
但这确实像是一场爆炸一样冲击了他们的领域。
But it's really, really come in just like an explosion to their field.

11
00:01:17,646 --> 00:01:19,880
所以他们正在试图弄清楚这对他们意味着什么。
And so they're trying to figure out what this means for them.

12
00:01:19,918 --> 00:01:30,960
但归根结底，我认为数学家通常被认为是地球上最聪明的人类，是那些从事纯数学研究的人。
But ultimately, mathematicians, I think, are generally regarded as being the
absolute smartest human beings on the planet, the ones who do pure mathematics.

13
00:01:31,930 --> 00:01:37,100
我们一直把他们的智慧留给这些极其困难的数学难题。
And we have reserved their minds to do these really, really hard math problems.

14
00:01:38,350 --> 00:01:40,004
我们已经这样做几千年了。
And we've done that for thousands of years.

15
00:01:41,006 --> 00:01:41,220
明白吗？
Okay?

16
00:01:41,340 --> 00:01:46,920
任何物理学家都会告诉你，在智力层级上，数学家比我们更高。
And any physicist will tell you the mathematicians are up on the hierarchy of intelligence compared to us.

17
00:01:47,182 --> 00:01:48,000
我们一致同意这一点。
We agree.

18
00:01:48,526 --> 00:01:49,000
明白吗？
Okay?

19
00:01:49,294 --> 00:02:00,880
突然人工智能出现了，它能解决一些原本属于他们专属领域的难题。
And suddenly they have artificial intelligence come in and it can do at least some of the problems that was exclusively their domain.

20
00:02:01,180 --> 00:02:02,840
所以这种冲击非常强烈。
So it's coming in hard.

21
00:02:03,534 --> 00:02:05,000
那么这对社会意味着什么呢？
So what does this mean for society?

22
00:02:05,320 --> 00:02:07,000
嗯，目前还不明确。
Well, unclear.

23
00:02:07,500 --> 00:02:11,880
它将带来变革，但同时也会造成很大的动荡。
It is going to be transformative, but also very disruptive.

24
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:15,240
当你习惯了某种做法时，你必须做出改变，我们必须转型。
When suddenly you're used to doing things, you're going to have to change, we're going to have to pivot.

25
00:02:15,420 --> 00:02:19,080
但我有信心，数学家在未来仍有作为。
And I'm confident mathematicians still have something to do in the future.

26
00:02:19,740 --> 00:02:22,436
哪怕只是做天文学，他们也能胜任，因为我们还有很多工作交给他们做。
They can do astronomy, if nothing else, because we have a lot of work for them.

27
00:02:23,150 --> 00:02:33,572
但最终，我认为我们必须去提醒自己：人工智能是人类构建的工具，是为了服务我们的。
But in the end, we have to go through, in my opinion, and remind ourselves
that artificial intelligence is a human construct there to serve us.

28
00:02:34,700 --> 00:02:47,428
所以我今天会用多种方式强调这一点：无论发生什么，人类的责任归属是我们思考的核心。
And so I will repeat this in many different forms today, that whatever happens,
human accountability is at the forefront of what we need to be thinking.

29
00:02:48,100 --> 00:02:49,540
人工智能不承担责任。
AI is not accountable.

30
00:02:50,580 --> 00:02:58,880
人类要为我们如何使用它负责，我们需要确保将这一点融
入到未来的发展中，因为据我目前所知，我们还没有做到。
Humans are accountable for how we use it, and we need to make sure we build
that into what happens, because right now, as near as I can tell, we are not.

31
00:03:00,206 --> 00:03:06,212
当有人利用人工智能做坏事时，必须有人类来承担责任，我们需要把这一点建立进去。
When you go in and do something bad with AI, a human needs to be responsible, and we need to build that in.

32
00:03:06,574 --> 00:03:07,980
布莱恩，非常感谢。
Brian, thank you very much indeed.

33
00:03:08,460 --> 00:03:16,500
苏仁，你从事可解释人工智能研究，并经常提到我们需要了解人工智能底层运行的逻辑。
So Su-In, you work on explainable AI and often talk of the need to understand what's going on under the hood of AI.

34
00:03:17,070 --> 00:03:18,180
请多讲一些。
Tell us more.

35
00:03:18,540 --> 00:03:28,324
是的，我的观点是，人工智能仍是一项不断发展的技术，它的未来并非预先注定的。
Yeah, so I think my view is that AI is still an evolving technology and its future is predetermined.

36
00:03:28,750 --> 00:03:29,580
远非如此。
It's far from it.

37
00:03:30,100 --> 00:03:41,360
而且我们正在积极塑造它的未来，通过我们选择去追
求的研究方向——尤其是像我这样的人工智能研究人员。
And then we are actively shaping the future of it And through research directions, we choose to pursue, well,
especially people like myself, AI researchers.

38
00:03:42,190 --> 00:03:56,900
这就是为什么我认为，开发能提高人工智能可解释性、问责制和可信度的新技术至关重要。
And this is why I believe that developing new technologies that can improve the interpretability of AI and also accountability and the
trustworthiness of AI is of paramount importance.

39
00:03:56,980 --> 00:04:16,060
我们需要新方法来帮助我们理解复杂的模型、理解其内部运作机制，
并帮助我们识别和解决这些复杂模型的故障模式。
And we need methods, new methods, that can help us understand the complex AI models, the complex inner workings of AI models,
and then also help us identify and also address the failure modes of these complex AI models.

40
00:04:16,781 --> 00:04:28,120
所以底线是，这项技术仍在不断进步，而我们如何推进它，取决于我们自己。
So the bottom line is that, you know, this is the technology that is still
advancing, and then it depends on us, you know, how we will move forward.

41
00:04:28,120 --> 00:04:38,788
因此，强调像我关注的这类技术——可解释性——是非常重要的。
And then it would be really important to put emphasis on, you know, this kind of technology, you know,
like the technology I'm focusing on: explainably.

42
00:04:39,534 --> 00:04:45,440
那么你会说，我们目前在回答“人工智能将走向何方”这个问题时过于消极吗？
So would you say that we are currently too passive in answering that question of where are we going with AI?

43
00:04:47,060 --> 00:04:57,740
不，我的意思是，并非一定要这样说，我只是想说，我
们不应该把当前的人工智能仅仅看作一个静态的东西。
No, I mean, not necessarily, I'm just saying that, you know, We just shouldn't consider this current AI as just a static thing, right?

44
00:04:57,860 --> 00:05:08,080
它是动态的，在不断变化，人类通过让它更易于理解和可解释来改进它是非常重要的。
It's dynamic, it keeps changing, and it's really important for humans
to make it better by making more understandable and interpretable.

45
00:05:08,558 --> 00:05:09,640
非常感谢。
Thank you very much indeed.

46
00:05:10,446 --> 00:05:11,680
尚旭，你是一位哲学家。
Sangwook, you're a philosopher.

47
00:05:11,920 --> 00:05:19,260
你评论说，随着人工智能的出现，科学家们比以前更渴望让哲学家参与到他们的讨论中。
You commented that now that with the advent of AI, scientists are rather keener
than they were before on having philosophers involved in their discussions.

48
00:05:19,260 --> 00:05:21,140
是的，相对而言，这是正确的。
Yeah, relatively speaking, that's right.

49
00:05:21,780 --> 00:05:23,040
那么，请你来谈谈……
So, here you are.

50
00:05:23,600 --> 00:05:25,220
你会如何……
How would you...

51
00:05:26,222 --> 00:05:28,196
毕竟，我的意思是，存在一些……
After all, I mean, there are...

52
00:05:28,520 --> 00:05:38,420
我想先同意其他嘉宾的观点，即我们对人工智能的开发
和部署存在巨大的不确定性，我们还有很多工作要做。
I would like to just agree with the other panellists that we have great
uncertainties about AI development and deployment and we have a lot to do.

53
00:05:39,040 --> 00:05:44,320
话虽如此，我认为在科学研究中，人工智能有两个不同的维度。
Having said that, I think there is two different dimensions of AI in scientific research.

54
00:05:44,462 --> 00:05:52,320
第一个是比较明确的问题，即用于科学研究的人工智能。
First one is rather non-controversial issues, which is AI for scientific research.

55
00:05:52,600 --> 00:06:03,140
所以，很多人都同意你的观点，即利用人工智能来提高科
学研究的生产力，也就是获取科学知识，是非常出色的。
So, many people agree with you that, you know, using AI actually productivity
of a scientific research, I mean, making scientific knowledge is excellent.

56
00:06:03,320 --> 00:06:06,440
我的意思是，它的提升非常惊人。
I mean, its improvement is really amazing.

57
00:06:06,440 --> 00:06:20,804
但第二点是相对有争议的，因为人工智能发展迅速，
人们越来越担心科学研究最终的目标会变成什么样。
But the second thing is, relatively controversial thing is, because AI is rapidly developing,
there are more and more concerns about what would be the kind of final goal of scientific research.

58
00:06:21,060 --> 00:06:28,540
以及从事这种获取科学知识工作的科学家的真实性问题。
and what would be the kind of authenticity of scientists who are doing this kind of making scientific knowledge.

59
00:06:28,558 --> 00:06:38,680
因此，目前有很多讨论在进行，即我们所谓的“科学研究”这类活动是否能继续维持现状。
And so, there are lots of discussions going on, whether the kind of activities we call scientific research can continue as it were.

60
00:06:39,660 --> 00:06:54,180
我的意思是，虽然在某些领域人工智能确实能更好地解决问题，
但这并不一定意味着我们必须将人工智能纳入我们的科学研究共同体中。
I mean, because given that there are some areas of scientific research where AI actually can serve the problems better,
but that doesn't necessarily mean that we have to include AI into our scientific research community.

61
00:06:54,240 --> 00:07:02,320
因为正如你所说，人工智能没有任何价值观判断，而且目前它们也不承担责任。
because as you said, the AI doesn't have any kind of value judgment, and they are not accountable at the moment.

62
00:07:02,740 --> 00:07:16,740
所以我们面临很多问题，需要更全面地去处理，或许可以邀请哲学家加入到这个科研讨论圈子里。
So there are lots of questions we have confronted which we have to work with in a more comprehensive way,
perhaps with philosophers into this research discussion community.

63
00:07:17,166 --> 00:07:21,508
你认为目前对科学研究目标的讨论是否足够充分？
Do you think there's enough discussion of what the goal of scientific research is?

64
00:07:21,540 --> 00:07:22,780
嗯……
Well,

65
00:07:22,780 --> 00:07:27,220
