00:11:52,366 --> 00:11:53,580
人类科学家，是的。
Human scientist, yeah.

103
00:11:53,800 --> 00:11:56,300
这取决于具体的科学领域。
So it depends on the science.

104
00:11:56,480 --> 00:12:05,560
我的意思是，人工智能的优势在于可扩展性、自主性，而且它处理任务的速度肯定比人类快。
I mean, AI has the strength in scalability, the autonomy, certainly it does things faster than humans.

105
00:12:05,720 --> 00:12:18,800
而人类目前擅长识别哪些问题更重要，至少在我所在的
生物科学或医学领域，人类仍然知道哪些问题是关键。
And the humans currently are good at identifying what problems are important, at least in the scientific field I'm at,
biological science or medicine, still humans know which problems are important.

106
00:12:19,220 --> 00:12:35,180
所以我认为这是我们目前的现状，但如果看长远一点的未
来，我认为教育是一个非常重要的点，我们需要深入思考。
So I think that's currently where we are, but if we see the longer term future,
I think education is a really important point we really need to think about.

107
00:12:35,406 --> 00:12:46,720
也就是说，我们该如何让下一代科学家以及更广泛的社会，
去适应一个日益受到人工智能影响的世界。
You know, how we should prepare the next generation of scientists and
society more broadly for a world that's increasingly shaped by AI.

108
00:12:47,246 --> 00:12:56,840
所以我认为，其中一项非常重要的技能——无论是对科学家还是非
科学领域的专业人士都适用——就是了解人工智能是如何运作的。
So I think, you know, one of the skills that's really important, this is
applied to scientists and then non-scientists, you know, how AI works.

109
00:12:57,880 --> 00:13:03,700
你看，现在的人工智能基本上就是从数据中学习统计规律。
You know, the modern AI is basically, it learns statistical patterns from the data.

110
00:13:04,240 --> 00:13:09,520
所以人类得知道它是怎么运作的，它能做什么，不能做什么，以及它可能在哪出错。
So humans should know how it works, what it can do, what it cannot do, and then how it can fail.

111
00:13:10,060 --> 00:13:16,720
除了那些识别重要问题的科学家技能之类的。
So other than, you know, scientist skills, you know, to identify important problems and so on.

112
00:13:17,200 --> 00:13:20,900
但对于年轻一代来说，我认为重要的技能是……
but for younger generation, I think important skill is, you know.

113
00:13:20,900 --> 00:13:31,700
所以人工智能素养加上扎实的统计基础，我认为应该是教育的基础部分。
So this AI literacy along with solid statistical foundation, I think it should be a fundamental part of education.

114
00:13:33,166 --> 00:13:36,560
就像学习数学和语言一样。
You know, a lot like, you know, learning math and then our languages.

115
00:13:37,220 --> 00:13:37,620
谢谢。
Thank you.

116
00:13:37,760 --> 00:13:38,212
罗恩，简单说一下。
Ron, briefly.

117
00:13:38,420 --> 00:13:38,560
好的。
Yeah.

118
00:13:38,640 --> 00:13:49,200
在最高层面上，你得处于一个能确保人工智能是你的工具，
并且你对它在任何工作中的表现负责的位置。
At the very highest level, you need to be positioned to make sure that
AI is your slave and you're accountable for what it does in whatever job.

119
00:13:49,582 --> 00:13:53,720
如果你是个水管工，你就得确保你掌控全局。
If you're going to be a plumber, then you need to make sure you're in charge of what happens.

120
00:13:53,940 --> 00:13:55,620
那可能挺稳妥的，水管工程。
That's probably pretty safe, plumbing.

121
00:13:56,440 --> 00:14:00,280
如果你是计算机科学家，那你就得确保你掌握主动权。
If you are a computer scientist, then you've got to make sure you're in charge of things.

122
00:14:00,480 --> 00:14:09,340
所以我认为在最高层面上，确保你掌控人工智能，而不
是让它随心所欲地替你做事，这是人们需要学习的技能。
So I think at the very highest level, making sure you're in charge of AI
and it doesn't just do stuff for you is the skill that people need to learn.

123
00:14:10,680 --> 00:14:11,300
我
I

124
00:14:11,300 --> 00:14:29,040
从历史角度看，去技能化在我们的科学研究史上一直存在。例如，在19世纪，
每位科学家都必须自己制造机器来进行实验，但我们现在不再这样做。
think, historically speaking, de-skilling always happens in our science research history because, for instance, in the 19th century,
every scientist has to build their own machine in order to make an experiment, but we don't do that anymore.

125
00:14:29,320 --> 00:14:47,320
所以去技能化本身不是大问题，问题在于，正如你提到的，
我们必须专注于哪些技能需要持续维护和培训，即使这些技能可以被人工智能自动化。
So de-skilling itself is not a big problem, but the problem is, as you mentioned,
we have to focus what kind of skills we have to maintain and train continuously, even when those skills can be automated by AI.

126
00:14:47,630 --> 00:14:53,380
因为其中一些技能与责任、问责制和伦理判断有关。
Because some of the skills are related to the responsibility, accountability, and ethical judgment.

127
00:14:53,580 --> 00:15:01,572
我们需要专注于这类技能，才能继续作为一名真正有能力的科学家工作。
And we need to focus on this kind of skill to keep on working as a real competent scientist.

128
00:15:01,998 --> 00:15:03,180
非常感谢。
Thank you very much indeed.

129
00:15:03,278 --> 00:15:04,300
谢谢各位。
